in 1983 and is headquartered in Chicago, Illinois. Array Digital Infrastructure, Inc. is a subsidiary of Telephone and Data Systems, Inc.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Anthony J. M. Carlson | President, CEO & Director | Age 38 | Compensation: $406,692 (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 60 people. Revenue per employee of $2.7M ranks in the top quartile among Communication Services peers, declining at 19%/yr \u2014 weakening productivity. Each employee generates $2.9M of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $30K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 0\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (6/10).","financial_summary":["Array Digital Infrastructure, I is a mid-cap communication services business with a $2.6B market cap on $163M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -66% over the past three years and -27% annually across the full decade, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome. Operating margins are contracting by -4.1pp, the first warning that competitive pressure is eroding the franchise.","Returns on capital run at 0% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $174M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 107 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 4.12\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, thin -3.3\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.8%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 72% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Op